DTSTART:20261115T222900Z
DTEND:20261115T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Witte Rook x IZOLYATSIA: Digital Explorers (Acr
 oss Borders) Online Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 15 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nWitte Rook (Breda) and the 
 Ukrainian platform IZOLYATSIA run Digital Explorers (Across Borders)\, a f
 ully online residency program exploring the artist-in-residence of the fut
 ure through cross-border collaboration. Each of three phases pairs one art
 ist from the Netherlands with one from Ukraine\, working together for abou
 t three months on the common.garden platform.\n\nOrganisation: Witte Rook 
 and IZOLYATSIA\nLocation: Online\, on the common.garden platform. Open to 
 artists living and working in the Netherlands or Ukraine. Organizers based
  in Breda (NL) and Ukraine.\nAward: EUR 1\,800 artist fee (excluding VAT) 
 plus EUR 1\,000 material budget (excluding VAT) per artist. Six artists se
 lected in total (three Dutch-Ukrainian pairs). No application fee.\nDurati
 on: Approximately three months per phase: Phase 1 'Form' (January to March
  2027)\, Phase 2 'Content' (May to July 2027)\, Phase 3 'Analysis' (Septem
 ber to December 2027).\n\nMore: https://witterook.nl/agenda/open-call-digi
 tal-explorers/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://witterook.nl/agenda/open-call-digital-explorers/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, on the common.garden platform. Open to artists living and
  working in the Netherlands or Ukraine. Organizers based in Breda (NL) and
  Ukraine.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261105T195128Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastrich
 t\, 11 months)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Jan van Eyck Academie's
  general open call for its 2028 residency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curator
 s\, designers\, writers\, architects and other artistic researchers spend 
 11 months (15 January to 15 December 2028) in Maastricht\, across material
 -based and research-driven practices\, with access to the academy's labs a
 nd community.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van Eyck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht
 \, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settle in Maastricht an
 d register with the municipality (the academy applies for visas where rele
 vant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants 
 with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo member or EUR 2\,500 combined for life 
 partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined\, max three stipends)\, w
 ith rent including service costs deducted from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,
 000 annual working budget and a newly built\, furnished private studio apa
 rtment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived fo
 r applicants from and living in OECD DAC-list countries\; enrolment fee fo
 r accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl. VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 Ja
 nuary to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 positions\; selection outcome mid-May
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency
 -2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
